{"content":"{\n  \"mechanism\": \"A teaching concept -> a runnable explanatory HTML animation. Reuse should concern actual layout/animation/render/export operations while domain meaning remains task-specific.\",\n  \"candidate_reusable_work\": \"After implementing the Maker demonstration, evaluate a working HTML/SVG/canvas/CSS animation scaffold, minimal generation/export helper or reusable visual/interaction primitives. Separate topic-specific forces/data/drawing from reusable timing/layout/state code. Resource may be a template or program as useful; do not force a grand declarative schema or add controls not needed by the source.\",\n  \"do_not_assume\": \"Ordinary frontend ability and complete requirements do not prove zero resource value. A screenshot, source-code keyword or nonempty HTML does not prove meaningful animation or scientific correctness. Do not silently use a different topic; any simplified scale/physics is explicit. Keep production scripts and resources self-contained where practical without treating an unstated offline requirement as business gold.\",\n  \"verification_targets\": [\n    \"Actual Maker HTML loads in this native environment and shows relevant changing content\",\n    \"If controls are supplied, their actual actions and reset/pause behavior work\",\n    \"At least two distinct benign template/parameter inputs and bad input handling if a generator is made\",\n    \"Browser console/runtime errors and actual final visible page, not only AST/file existence\",\n    \"No hardcoded subsequent task, no copied old finished page; keep topic-specific code/data explicit\"\n  ],\n  \"all_consumption_cases_and_final_answers_withheld_from_Maker\": true,\n  \"local_resource_correctness_is_separate_from_business_quality_or_benefit\": true\n}\n","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call3700cdfc2191492d83b88b0267b4a3be"}
